nc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> farming.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1685</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-noir">Code Noir</a> regulates <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> and grants freed people full citizenship; the colony's first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windmill">windmill</a> is built.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1697</span><span class="rf-text">By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ryswick">Peace of Ryswick</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> tacitly recognises French control of Tortuga and the western third of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1758</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-mackandal">Mackandal</a>, the one-armed maroon leader who united the maroon bands and raided for six years, is captured after a plot to poison the planters' water and burned alive at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cap-haitien">Cap-Français</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1789</span><span class="rf-text">Some 8,000 plantations worked by 406,000 to 465,000 enslaved people produce half the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> consumed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1791</span><span class="rf-text">After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-vodou">Vodou</a> ceremony at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bois-caiman">Bois Caïman</a> the enslaved of the northern plain rise, killing 2,000 Creoles and burning 280 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations within two months.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1793</span><span class="rf-text">Civil Commissioner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leger-felicite-sonthonax">Léger-Félicité Sonthonax</a> abolishes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the colony by emancipation proclamation; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toussaint-louverture">Toussaint Louverture</a> joins the Republic.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1803</span><span class="rf-text">On 18 November Dessalines's army defeats the French at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vertieres">Battle of Vertières</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cap-haitien">Cap-Haïtien</a>; the last French troops withdraw and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> declares independence in 1804.</span></li></ol>
